PATCH 581: the glyph vector's word width (02e8/02c5/5531), the fire-mission subtasks (b040's segment
and its four handlers), five render methods c4df dispatched into the void, the model-budget vector 4397,
the map inset's walk (8e80, 7f32, the 9f70 shade LUT), op 0x2c's texel walk (9129), the night raycaster
(6c00) and the divide-error handler at two extender divisions.

board:0002 / board:0015 / board:0017.  Found with the trap trace (FIST_TRACE_TRAPS now prints the tick
and a native backtrace; FIST_TRAP_BREAK=<linear> stops gdb at one target) on AZER1 after the gate
rewrite, and by comparing the port's frames with the oracle's pass-8 capture:

  02e8/02c5  the number printers save/restore the glyph vector [0x684]:[0x686] around 541b.  The port's
         DAT_1000_c684 accessor is 4 bytes wide, so `[0x684] = save684` wrote 0 over the segment
         [0x686] just restored: after every readout the vector read 0000:19ae and the next drawstring
         dispatched into segment 0 -- no ammo digits, no PL:UN box, no GOALS REMAINING.  02c5 (the
         near twin) had also lost its pop pair to `[0x684] = [0x686] ; [0x686] = CS`.  5531 (the
         far-entry drawstring) now hands the MGA glyph method its character like the 552b thunk does.
  b040   the fire-mission subtask dispatcher runs in the 0f69 cluster: `cs:[si-0x4637]` is the table
         {b9d1 b9d2 b9f1 ba0e} at 0x1b059, 0f69-relative.  Patch 260 based it on CS=0x1000, read the
         data word 0xf6c2 and trapped; the four states (idle, the 0x258-tick cooldown, the fuse, the
         artillery spawn -- b1df type 0x16 at the target scattered by ((b26a&0xff)-0x80)<<6, grounded
         by adcd) are emitted as FUN_1000_b061/b062/b081/b09e and take BX (the record) as their arg.
  c783/c845/c862/c876/c888  the render methods of the view-0x20/0x1e/0x22 tables (STRSEG:0x35fa /
         0x3632 / 0x35c2) for classes 0x1a/0x1b and the view-0x22 vehicles: sprite selection by the
         object's flags, the blinking draw c894, `stc` for the skips.  None was emitted.
  4397   the model budget: `sub [0x6d9d],ax ; jb` charges every mesh of the STRSEG:0x802 loader
         table against the paragraphs 42cc reserved (patch 571); exhausted -> the CRT's message
         services and CF=1 (or the [0x58] restart for BX=0xb93).  Trapped before.
  8e80   op 0x5c's map walk (7990: the TCB's surface/size into 90ec/90f0/90f4/90f8, 85d0, 8e80, 79d7),
         8df0's unpromoted mid-entry: the heading's cos/sin rotate a top-down walk of the colormap
         through the shade LUT [0x85c4] into the inset surface.  7f32 (the platoon/objective marker
         blitter) based its destination on the linear 90ec; the LUT builder in 9f70 (`lea ebx,
         [edi*3+0x5260] ; al = [ebx]+[ebx+1]+[ebx+1]+[ebx+2] ; div 0x17`) indexed the sorted palette
         in dwords -- 256/256 LUT bytes now equal the oracle's.
  9129   op 0x2c's texel walk (0x8460 = 8120 ; 9130 ; 82d0), 9200's twin with a 50 % blend: the
         self-modified sampler displacement read from [0x3918], the horizon table as an image offset.
  6c00   the NIGHT raycaster (3931's other branch, [0x395d] = TCB+0xcf): 6980 with its own
         self-modified sites and `sub al,0x50 ; shr al,2 ; add al,0x50` on every terrain texel.
         Ghidra's own 6c00 kept the host-address table reads; AZER3 and twelve other night
         battles crashed on their first frame.
  85d0/395e  `div ecx` / `idiv ebx` with a zero divisor (a zero focal once the view's vehicle is gone,
         a zero ramp product): the extender routes #DE to the engine's INT-0 handler 0f69:5b36,
         which steps past the DIV and returns AX = 0xffff with EAX otherwise untouched -- EAX =
         0xffffffff.  Modelled at both sites.

  Measured (AZER1 frame 8 against oracle_9200_framematched_pass08.png): 96.3 % of the frame
  pixel-identical, the map inset 97.9 %, the ammo readouts 0015/0020/2000/0005 as the original's.

